        "contenuto_esteso": "Israel sends UAE laser weapon called âIron Beamâ - What it means in face of Iranian drones and why is it important TOI World Desk / TIMESOFINDIA.COM / May 02, 2026, 10:41 IST Comments AA Small Medium Large Israel has supplied the United Arab Emirates with an advanced laser-based air defence system, known as âIron Beamâ, as tensions escalate amid the ongoing US-Iran conflict. The system, designed to vapourise short-range rockets and drones, marks a major step in defence cooperation between the two countries and signals a deepening strategic partnership in West Asia. According to a report by Financial Times, Israel deployed a version of its Iron Beam system to help the UAE counter Iranian missile and drone attacks. The laser system was previously used by Israel against Hezbollah projectiles from Lebanon and is capable of intercepting threats at short range with high precision. Turkeyâs New AI âMizrakâ Drone Makes Big Debut; 1000 Km Range Puts Israel In Striking Target | Watch Israel also sent an advanced surveillance system, âSpectroâ, which can detect incoming drones from up to 20 kilometres away. Reports indicate that several of the systems deployed were still in prototype stages and not fully integrated into Israelâs own defence network, underscoring the urgency of the situation. A regional official described the move as a display of \"the value of being Israel's friend\". Another source familiar with the deployment said Israel rushed systems âoff the bench and gave it to the Emiratisâ, while a third individual remarked, \"We let them into our underwear\". The UAE reportedly faced a barrage of more than 500 ballistic missiles and 2,000 drones from Iran. In response, layered air defence systems, including Israeli equipment, were activated, successfully intercepting a majority of incoming threats. Israeli personnel were also deployed to assist operations on the ground. US clears $8.6bn arms deals for allies Amid rising regional instability, the United States has approved military sales worth over $8.6 billion to key allies including Israel, Qatar, Kuwait and the UAE, according to Al Jazeera. The deals include a $4 billion Patriot missile system sale to Qatar and nearly $1 billion in precision-guided weapons for Israel. The US State Department said the agreements aim to strengthen allied defence capabilities and support broader regional security objectives. Congress retains the authority to review the proposed sales. US President Donald Trump defended the military campaign against Iran, dismissing criticism of its effectiveness. âWe get the radical left to say, 'We're not winning, we're not winning.' They don't have any military left. It's unbelievable,â he said. âIt's actually, it's actually, I believe it's treasonous, okay. You want to know the truth, it's treasonous.â Trump claimed Iranâs military capabilities had been severely weakened. âAnd Iran is getting decimated. They have no navy. They have no air force. They have no anti-aircraft equipment. They have no radar. They have no leaders; their leaders are all gone,â he said. Deepening Israel-UAE defence ties The deployment highlights the growing military relationship between Israel and the UAE following the Abraham Accords, brokered by the United States. The accords formally established diplomatic ties and opened the door for expanded defence and economic cooperation. Israel has previously supplied the UAE with Barak and Spyder air defence systems, but the current conflict marks the first major operational test of this partnership. A western official noted that the UAE became a primary Iranian target partly due to its âenthusiasticâ embrace of the accords. The transfer of cutting-edge systems like Iron Beam reflects both the intensity of the conflict and the strategic importance of the Israel-UAE alliance in countering regional threats. End of Article Tired of too many ads? go ad free now Arsenal Missiles Tanks Guns Submarines RS-28 Sarmat Satan II Missiles RS-28 Sarmat Satan II Russia Trident II D5 USA LGM-30G Minuteman III USA RS-24 Yars Russia M51.3 France Agni-V India Hwasong-17 N. Korea RT-2PM2 Topol-M Russia Julang-2 China Agni-V India Agni-P India K-4 India BrahMos India Pralay India Nirbhay India Akash-NG India Astra Mk2 India Rudram-1 India MR-SAM India Iron Dome Tamir Israel David's Sling Stunner Israel Arrow 2 Israel Arrow 3 Israel Jericho III Israel LORA Israel Delilah Israel Popeye Turbo ALCM Israel Spike NLOS Israel Python 5 Israel Derby Israel Patriot PAC-3 MSE USA THAAD USA SM-3 Block IIA USA SM-6 USA Tomahawk Block V USA JASSM-ER USA AIM-120D AMRAAM USA BGM-109 Tomahawk Block IV USA Shahab-3 Iran Emad Iran Sejjil-2 Iran Kheibar Shekan Iran Fattah-1 Iran Soumar Iran Paveh Iran Noor Iran Khalij Fars Iran Shahed-136 Iran Bavar-373 Iran Fateh-110 Iran Russia Missile RS-28 Sarmat Satan II Service Start 2023 Service End Present Range 18000 km Compare Across Missiles Defence Videos 08:03 Iran Expands War Threat: Bab Al Mandeb, Aramco, Yanbu, Fujairah Now In Direct Conflict Line 10:57 Iran Rejects Talks After US Fires On Sanctioned Cargo Ship Touska, Says âBlockade Main Obstacleâ 08:01 NATO IS DEAD? Europe KICKS U.S. Out of 'NEW SECRET BLOC' Amid Trump's Exit Threat Over Iran War 10:05 Nearly 400 U.S. Soldiers Injured In Iran War, Reveals CENTCOM; America Hiding Losses? Defence News Defence | 2 hours ago Dolphins on duty? How Iran could deploy trained mine-carriers against the US Navy Defence | 18 hours ago Peru to buy 12 F-16s: Why a fighter that first flew 50 years ago still dominates the skies Defence | a day ago Russia test launches Soyuz-5 rocket with âworldâs most powerful liquid-fuelled engineâ Defence | a day ago Navy gets stealth frigate Mahendragiri: All you need to know about state-of-the art warship"
